president biden is beginning a four-day  visit to the middle east planning to  meet with leaders of israel the  palestinian authority and saudi arabia  all with an eye on regional rival iran  and ed o'keefe has made his way to  jerusalem traveling with the president  this is the president's second stop on  his tour of that region ed good morning  to you  what's in store for the president over  the next few days  tony good to see you the white house  points out this is the president's tenth  trip to israel over the course of his  career his first as commander-in-chief  he's set to arrive here in about an hour  and we'll get a look at israel's  anti-missile defense systems and later  make a visit to the country's national  holocaust memorial but broadly over the  course of this week it's about warning  and isolating iran and its nuclear  ambitions here in israel he's set to  unveil a new joint u.s and israel  agreement committing to never allow iran  to get a nuclear weapon both countries  set to say they'll use all of their  power to stop that from happening and  notably ahead of the president's arrival  russia's president vladimir putin  announced he will visit iran next week  that comes as the biden administration  says iran is set to give russia armed  drones for its invasion of ukraine once  he leaves israel on friday the president  is set to go to saudi arabia to attend a  regional conference and meet with that  country's king and its controversial  crown prince mohammed bin salman  gail  he raised a lot of eyebrows over that  one thank you very much ed o'keefe
 

